- op: discuss  # 87af
  at: '2026-08-17T11:04:23Z'  # 87af
  by: agent  # 87af
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 87af
  clock: 4  # 87af
  nonce: 87af  # 87af
  message: "MEAS-1 CORRECTION — the pass/non-pass split recorded on this item and on WI-balaf was\ncomputed with a metric that does not sum to the wall clock, so the earlier\n\"analyzers 22% / linkers 7% / overhead 71%\" numbers overstate the pass share.\n\nSumming per-pass duration_ms treats concurrent passes as if they were serial. On\nhypergumbo itself: 96 cards total 157.7s of duration_ms, but the run_all_analyzers +\nrun_all_linkers spans measured 93.9s of WALL. Card sums are closer to CPU time than\nto elapsed, so any \"share of wall\" derived from them is inflated, and the residual\nattributed to non-pass overhead by subtraction is correspondingly understated in\nkind (though it was still the dominant term).\n\nWall-clock shares from direct phase timing (scripts/measure-survey-phase-split.py,\ninclusive/exclusive accounting, reconciling to 95.7%):\n    analyzers 12.6%  |  linkers 5.6%  |  fingerprint post-pass 62.6%\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THIS ITEM'S BASELINE TABLE. The cells recorded here (33s / 119s /\n201s / 489s cold full analysis) are wall-clock and remain valid as totals. What is\nNOT valid is decomposing any of them via card sums. If MEAS-1 wants a per-phase\ndecomposition per repo, the phase-split instrument produces one directly, and its\n--lean arm additionally prices the side outputs.\n\nAlso relevant to the band decision rule: after the WI-balaf fix a cold full analysis\nof this monorepo is 220.0s, not 517.7s. The rule keys on measured wall clock, so\nre-read it against the new figure rather than the old one."  # 87af
