  clock: 6  # fd61
  nonce: fd61  # fd61
  message: "OWNER RULING (2026-08-17), verbatim: \"I guess we've mined all the processing\nefficiency that's reasonable to mine at this point in the hypergumbo project.\"\n\nPARKED — wont_do + someday. Not \"won't ever\"; \"not at this point in the project\".\nThis item is intact and its ceiling is measured, so re-opening is a status change,\nnot a re-derivation.\n\nWHAT WAS ACTUALLY MINED, so nobody re-measures it:\n  cold run_survey on this monorepo   517.7s -> 139.1s   (3.7x)\n    #394  fingerprint locator was quadratic in file size   -297.7s (62.6% of wall)\n    #395  --minimal declines side outputs a caller never reads   -59.1s\n    #397  one shared CLI scan instead of four                    -23.3s\n\nWHY PARKED. MEAS-1 existed to decide whether full-run latency hurt enough to\njustify the incremental designs. That question is now ANSWERED by other means and\nthe designs are parked, so the remaining cells (a real large single-repo cell,\nrepeat trials) would be measurement without a decision attached.\n\nWHAT SURVIVES AND SHOULD NOT BE LOST: the band rule, and the correction that its\nown numbers must not be decomposed via per-pass duration_ms sums (WI-nuvam). Any\nfuture latency question should start from scripts/measure-survey-phase-split.py,\nwhich reconciles to the wall clock, rather than re-running this item's protocol.\n\nRE-OPEN TRIGGER: a new latency complaint on a repo class not represented in the\nrecorded cells (33s / 119s / 201s / 489s-now-139.1s)."  # fd61
